               <description>A focal seizure originates within networks limited to one hemisphere. They may be discretely localized or more widely distributed. Focal seizures may originate in subcortical structures. Focal seizures are optionally subdivided into focal aware and focal impaired awareness seizures. Specific motor and nonmotor classifiers may be added. (Source: Fisher ea 2017, Table 2 and Key Points; Suggested tags from Fisher ea 2017, Figure 2; Beniczky ea 2017, Supplement 1, ILAE seizure classification code I.)</description>
